<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ganzak</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ganzak was the capital of the kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/media-atropatene">Media Atropatene</a> and later a major city of Sasanian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a>, in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>. It lay near the sanctuary of the sacred fire <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adur-gushnasp">Adur Gushnasp</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/takht-e-soleyman">Takht-e Soleyman</a>. The Byzantine emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heraclius">Heraclius</a> captured it in 624, and its exact site is still debated.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ganzak.jpg" alt="Ganzak" width="320" height="181" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Aivazovsky, heavily edited by HistoryofIran · CC BY-SA 1.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:AtropateneHistoryofIran.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
